# Environment variables
#
# The current code (Milestones 1–5 + follow-ups + public AI chat) needs the Supabase values
# for /login and /dashboard. The public site still runs without them, and the
# dashboard shows a setup notice instead.
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the Supabase section.
#
# AI, cron, email and WhatsApp variables are documented for later milestones.
# The public AI receptionist DOES read OPENAI_API_KEY and OPENAI_MODEL; if either is
# missing the assistant stays visibly not connected. Email, WhatsApp and cron
# variables are still not read by the app.
#
# Rules:
# - Never commit `.env.local` or real secrets.
# - Only NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are exposed to the browser.
# - Service-role, AI and notification keys must stay server-side.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Public site URL, used for absolute links and metadata.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (Milestone 2)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase Dashboard -> "Connect" dialog, or Project Settings -> API Keys.
# The publishable key (`sb_publishable_...`) is safe in the browser because RLS
# protects every table. The secret key (`sb_secret_...`) bypasses RLS and must
# NEVER be prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ or imported into client components.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Legacy key names. Still supported and still valid, but Supabase is deprecating
# them by the end of 2026. Use one pair or the other, not both.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI receptionist (Milestone 7)
# Both values are required for the public assistant. Keys are server-side only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Required when OPENAI_API_KEY is set. Example: gpt-4o-mini
OPENAI_MODEL=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=

# Reminder and feedback cron authentication (Milestone 9).
# Required to call POST/GET /api/cron/remind. Keep it server-side and unpredictable.
CRON_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email notifications (Milestone 9, planned Resend)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
RESEND_API_KEY=
# NOTIFICATION_FROM_EMAIL=
# NOTIFICATION_REPLY_TO=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WhatsApp notifications (Milestone 9, provider not selected yet)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHATSAPP_API_TOKEN=
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=
